# 30-Rust-Style: Implementation Standards

Follow idiomatic Rust patterns and repository conventions.

## Core Guidance
- [Implementation Patterns](file:///Users/antonio.ventilii/projects/icdc-core/.agents/patterns.md): Mandatory coding patterns.
- [General Instructions](file:///Users/antonio.ventilii/projects/icdc-core/.agents/instructions.md): Low-level coding rules.
- [Domain Logic](file:///Users/antonio.ventilii/projects/icdc-core/.agents/domain_logic.md): Bounded context and atomicity rules.

## Standards
- **Idiomatic Rust**: Prefer standard library types and avoid unsafe unless necessary.
- **Error Handling**: Use explicit error types; avoid `unwrap()` or `expect()`.
- **Snake Case**: All functions and variables must use `snake_case`.
- **Atomic Edits**: Targeted changes using specific lines or blocks.
